= Comer

[? if ch_res = "conv_limpio" : It takes eleven minutes and nobody is hurt, including the drivers, who are put face down in the ditch and then helped up and given back their papers and their cigarettes and pointed at Coyuca. The column eats the army's rations for six weeks off the army's account. And in Coyuca three men tell the story of the guerrillas who stopped a convoy and did not shoot anybody, which will be worth more to you next year than the flour. ?][? if ch_res = "conv_rapido" : It takes ninety seconds and you have everything, and two of the drivers do not get up. They were contract men from Coyuca in civilian shirts. Their families are in a town where the movement has been carefully building something for three years, and it will take a great deal longer than three years to build it back, and there is not one person in that town who is going to be interested in the distinction between the escort and the men driving the trucks. The column eats extremely well for six weeks. ?][? if ch_res = "conv_mal" : It goes wrong in the first fifteen seconds, the way it does when hungry men with eight rounds each try to take an escorted convoy, and you come off that road with a third of one truck and three fewer people. The column eats for two weeks. The army knows precisely how hungry you are, because starving men attack convoys, and now they know to watch the roads and wait. ?][? if ch_res = "isidro" : San Isidro says yes, because San Isidro always says yes. Forty people in eleven houses hand over most of what was going to get them to March, and refuse to be thanked, and refuse the offer to take less, and one of the old men gets annoyed at being asked twice. The column eats. And there is a thing that will sit in the stomachs of everybody who was there for the rest of their lives, which is that you are now a guerrilla being fed by people who will be hungry in February because of it. This is where a movement starts to become the thing it is fighting, and it does not happen with a rifle. It happens exactly like this, politely, with everybody agreeing. ?][? if ch_res = "repartir" : You take a kilo here and two kilos there across eleven hamlets, which takes nine days of walking and produces about half of what one village could have given you in an afternoon. Nobody is stripped. Nobody's February is destroyed. The column stays thin and stays fed and stays, in the one way that is going to matter when this is over, *theirs* — because the difference between being supported and being requisitioned from is not a matter of quantity, it is a matter of whether anybody was ruined. ?][? if ch_res = "pagar" : You pay, at the market price, in cash, and the arguments about it are long and heated and eventually you win them by simply putting the money down and leaving. It is a lot of money. It is the difference between an army that lives among people and an army that lives off them, and it is the only reason there will still be food in this valley to ask for next year. ?][? if ch_res = "disp_pueblo_ok" : The wounded go into houses, one to a village, under floors and in back rooms and in one case in an actual church, and the sierra takes them in the way it has taken in fugitives since the Cristiada. Two of them are being fed better than the column is. When the band regathers in March all four are alive, and one of them has married the daughter of the house, which everyone agrees is the single best thing that has happened all year. ?][? if ch_res = "disp_pueblo_mal" : You put four wounded men into villages that did not have enough reason to keep them, and within five weeks three of them have been given up — not maliciously, not even really by a decision, just by the enormous pressure a garrison can put on forty frightened people. The column regathers in March and counts. This is what the water is actually for, and this is what it costs when it is shallow: not a defeat in the field, just four men who were alive in December. ?][? if ch_res = "disp_llevar" : Every group takes a wounded man, which makes every group slower and hungrier and more likely to be caught, and you do it anyway and say why out loud so that it is on the record: this column does not leave people. It costs food and weeks and it very nearly costs more. And it becomes, without anyone deciding it should, the thing the band knows about itself — the story people tell when they are trying to explain why they stayed. Armies are made of this. So, occasionally, are revolutions. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# LOS QUE SE VAN — desertion, and then one specific person.
# =====================================================================
@ev_desercion
title: Los que se van
new-page: true
face-image: img/Luciodeath.jpg
subtitle: When morale breaks, men vote with their feet
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_moral <= 35 and f_hombres >= 8 and time >= f_deserta_last + 3
priority: 6
frequency: 80
max-visits: 6
on-arrival: {! Q.f_deserta_last=Q.time; Q.ch_p1=""; Q.ch_p2=""; Q.ch_res=""; !}

= Los que se van

They start going in the night, and it is not the ones you would have guessed.

Not informers and not cowards — tired men who joined believing it would be shorter than this, who have buried more friends than they can name in one breath and eaten badly for two years and can no longer see the end of it from where they are standing. One of them leaves a note. One of them leaves his rifle cleaned and oiled, propped where it will be found, which is somehow worse.

Desertion is the sound a foco makes when its morale runs out. What you do in the next week decides whether the trickle is a trickle.

- @des_dejar: Let them go, with a handshake. A guerrilla held by force is a liability with a rifle. *(the band shrinks and hardens)*
- @des_perseguir: Send people after them. A deserter is a walking file and an example that spreads. *(stops the bleeding by fear; poisons everything)*
- @des_causa: Stop the war for a month. Rest them, feed them, bury the dead properly, and give them a reason. *(costs a season of momentum)*

@des_dejar
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos2.des_uno
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="dejar"; Q.f_hombres-=4; Q.f_moral+=4; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+3; !}

@des_perseguir
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos2.des_uno
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="perseguir"; Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+2; Q.f_hombres-=1; Q.f_moral-=8; Q.paranoia=(Q.paranoia||8)+12; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)-6; Q.apoyo_popular-=4; Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; !}

@des_causa
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos2.des_uno
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="causa"; Q.f_moral+=14; Q.f_comida-=6; Q.f_cerco+=6; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+3; !}

@des_uno
title: Melquiades
new-page: true
face-image: img/guerillas3.jpg

= Melquiades

And then there is the one that is actually the problem.

Melquiades has been here since before the beginning. He was in the schoolyard in Atoyac in 1967. He has carried you eleven kilometres with a bullet in your shoulder. He knows every cache, every safe house, every family that has ever fed this column, and the name of every single person in the organization including the ones in Mexico City.

He is forty-four years old and he has been sitting apart from everyone for three weeks, and this morning he asked to speak to you, and what he said was that he cannot do it any more. Not that he disagrees. Not that he has been got at. That he is finished, and he wants to go home to Tecpan and see his mother before she dies, and he is telling you rather than simply walking because after nine years he is not going to walk.

[? if ch_p1 = "perseguir" : He is also aware that you sent men after the others last week. He mentioned it. He was not making a threat; he was giving you information about what everyone now understands. ?]

- @des_u_ir: Let him go home. Everything he knows walks down the mountain with him, and you shake his hand. *(the whole organization in one man's memory, out in the world)*
- @des_u_quedar: Ask him to stay — not as a fighter. Let him run the camp, the stores, the school. *(you keep him and he keeps his dignity; he is still finished)*
- @des_u_lejos: Let him go, but not to Tecpan — out of the state entirely, with money and papers, where nobody can reach him. *(safest for everyone; he does not see his mother)*
- @des_u_no: He knows too much. He does not leave. *(say plainly what that means)*

@des_u_ir
go-to: foco_eventos2.des_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="ir"; !}

@des_u_quedar
go-to: foco_eventos2.des_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="quedar"; !}

@des_u_lejos
go-to: foco_eventos2.des_fin
choose-if: funds >= 8
unavailable-subtitle: Papers and a bus to Sinaloa and something to live on cost money the column does not have.
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="lejos"; Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)-8; !}

@des_u_no
go-to: foco_eventos2.des_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="no"; !}

@des_fin
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
var _p1=Q.ch_p1||"", _p2=Q.ch_p2||"", _apoyo=Q.apoyo_popular||0;
if(_p2==="ir"){
  var _seguro=(_apoyo*0.6) - ((Q.brutalidad||0)*6) - ((Q.estado_intel||0)*0.25) + ((_p1==="perseguir")?-14:8) + 20;
