= Tecpan

[? if ch_res = "ir_bien" : He goes home. He sees his mother, who lives another two years. He never says one word to anybody about any of it — not to the DFS men who come to the house twice, not to his brother, not on his own deathbed in 1991 — and the reason is not discipline or fear or ideology. It is that you shook his hand at the top of the trail and said thank you, and that in nine years the organization never once gave him a reason to be anything other than loyal to it. Everything the column ever did well was, in the end, an investment in mornings like this one. ?][? if ch_res = "ir_mal" : He goes home, and they are waiting in Tecpan, because of course they are — a man of forty-four with a nine-year hole in his life walks back into a town with a garrison in it. What they do to him takes four days.[? if ch_p1 = "perseguir" :  And he had already worked out that this column shoots people who leave, which meant that when they offered him the only future in which he lived, he had no reason on earth to refuse it. ?] Everything he knows, they now know: caches, houses, families, names, the whole architecture of nine years. It is the single worst intelligence loss of the war and it did not involve a traitor. It involved a tired man who wanted to see his mother. ?][? if ch_res = "quedar" : He stays, and the thing you offered him turns out to be the thing he actually needed: not to be asked to fight any more. He runs the camp. Within four months the stores are inventoried, the school has a timetable, the wounded are in a room with a roof that does not leak, and there is bread. He is happier than he has been in three years and he is still, in some way that will not repair, finished — but he is finished *here*, among people, doing something. Half of what an army is, is finding the right job for the person in front of you. ?][? if ch_res = "lejos" : He takes the papers and the money and the bus and he goes to Sinaloa, and he is safe, and everything he knows is safe with him, and he does not see his mother again. She dies in the March. Somebody sends word. It is the correct decision by every measure available to a person responsible for forty other lives, and he understood it perfectly, and he did not forgive it, and there is no version of this in which everybody gets what they should have. ?][? if ch_res = "no" : You have him killed, because of what is in his head.[? if ch_p1 = "causa" :  Four weeks after stopping the entire war to remind everyone why they were here. ?] There is a military logic to it that is not even slightly wrong: he knew everything, and a man who has decided to leave is a man the state can eventually reach. And there is not one person in that column who will ever again believe they can say they are tired. What you have built, as of this morning, is an organization that people cannot leave — and every organization that people cannot leave becomes, within about eighteen months, an organization nobody is honest inside. He was in the schoolyard in 1967. So were you. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# HAN ENCONTRADO EL CAMPAMENTO — the address you spent years not having.
# =====================================================================
@ev_campamento_hallado
title: Han encontrado el campamento
new-page: true
face-image: img/campfound.jpg
subtitle: The one fixed thing you owned
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_campamento = 1 and camp_visto = 1 and time >= camp_last + 6
priority: 9
frequency: 90
max-visits: 4
on-arrival: {! Q.camp_last=Q.time; Q.ch_p1=""; Q.ch_p2=""; Q.ch_res=""; !}

= Han encontrado el campamento

It was always going to happen. The only question was whether you would be in it when it did.

A spotter plane goes over three times in a week on exactly the same line. Then a patrol turns up on a ridge that no patrol has any business knowing about. Then a boy comes up the arroyo at a dead run to say that the soldiers in Atoyac are asking very specific questions about a very specific fold in the sierra, and that one of the questions had a number in it.

The address you spent four years not having is now a grid reference in a file. Everything in the camp — the hospital, the stores, the school, the printing frame, two years of work — is now a thing with a date on it.

- @cam_defender: **Defenderlo.** This is ours; they do not simply walk into it. *(a battle on ground they have chosen and mapped)*
- @cam_levantar: **Levantarlo.** Take what can be carried, burn the rest, and be a homeless band again. *(the correct answer; it feels like defeat)*
- @cam_trampa: **Dejarlo minado.** Empty it, leave it looking lived-in, and wait on the ridges. *(needs materiel and nerve)*

@cam_defender
new-page: true
choose-if: f_hombres >= 16
unavailable-subtitle: Defending a fixed position against a formation needs at least 16 fighters.
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="defender"; !}

= Las posiciones

If you are going to do the one thing the manual forbids, you may as well do it properly. Three days to prepare, and the shape of the defence is a choice about what the camp is actually for.

- @cam_d_todo: Fortify everything — the hospital, the stores, the school. Nothing is given up. *(a wide perimeter with the men you have)*
- @cam_d_nucleo: Give up the outbuildings. Hold the high ground and the cave, and let them have the sheds. *(a small hard position; you lose the school before it starts)*

@cam_d_todo
go-to: foco_eventos2.cam_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="todo"; !}

@cam_d_nucleo
go-to: foco_eventos2.cam_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="nucleo"; !}

@cam_levantar
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="levantar"; !}

= Levantar

The order nobody wants and everybody knows is right. Maize onto backs, parque into caches nobody writes down, the doctor's instruments into a sack, and the rest burns behind you.

Except there is more than can be carried, and somebody has to decide what the column is.

- @cam_l_armas: The parque and the food. You are a fighting column and you have to be able to fight. *(the hospital and the school burn)*
- @cam_l_hospital: The hospital and the printing frame — the things that made this more than a band with rifles. *(you march out light on ammunition)*
- @cam_l_pueblo: Neither. Give the stores to the villages before you burn anything, and walk out with nothing. *(you have nothing; the valley has everything)*

@cam_l_armas
go-to: foco_eventos2.cam_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="armas"; !}

@cam_l_hospital
go-to: foco_eventos2.cam_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="hospital"; !}

@cam_l_pueblo
go-to: foco_eventos2.cam_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="pueblo"; !}

@cam_trampa
new-page: true
choose-if: f_parque >= 10 and disciplina >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: An ambush on your own home needs 10 parque and a column disciplined enough to lie still while soldiers walk through its kitchen.
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="trampa"; Q.f_parque-=10; !}

= Dejarlo puesto

Cooking fires banked. Blankets thrown as if slept in. A pot still warm on the ashes, which is the detail that will make it work or not.

- @cam_t_paciencia: Wait until they are all inside, spread out, comfortable, looking through your things. *(the maximum result; the maximum time lying still)*
- @cam_t_pronto: Take them at the perimeter the moment the first section commits. *(smaller; far less can go wrong)*

@cam_t_paciencia
go-to: foco_eventos2.cam_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="paciencia"; !}

@cam_t_pronto
go-to: foco_eventos2.cam_fin
