!}

= Lo que quedó

[? if ch_res = "def_todo_ok" : They come up the draw at first light and find that the fold in the sierra has been waiting for them since Tuesday. The fields of fire were cut months ago, the villages gave you three days' warning, and by noon the army is going back down the mountain having left equipment and a great deal of its confidence in the arroyo. The hospital still stands. The school still stands. A guerrilla that can *hold ground* is an entirely different order of problem, and every garrison in Guerrero now has to think about it. ?][? if ch_res = "def_nucleo_ok" : You give them the sheds and hold the rock, and that is the whole battle: they spend two hours taking a woodstore and a kitchen at a price they will have to explain, and then they look up at a cave mouth with a machine gun in it and decide that today is not the day. You lose the school building and the lower ramadas. You keep the cave, the stores, the wounded and the column. Anybody who has ever defended anything would recognize the trade instantly, and it is still hard to watch them burn the benches. ?][? if ch_res = "def_mal" : They came with more than you had, which is what they always do, and this time you were standing on a fixed point waiting for them. The camp is taken and burned: hospital, stores, school, printing frame, the lot. What breaks out through the trees is carrying its wounded and nothing else. You defended a fixed position against an army — the one thing the manual tells you never to do — and it cost the base and the best of the band, and every single person who told you so beforehand has the grace not to mention it. ?][? if ch_res = "lev_armas" : Parque and food, and everything else burns. The instruments go into the fire with the benches, which means the doctor's work is over, and he watches it and says nothing at all. You march out able to fight, which is what a fighting column is for, and the thing that was starting to make this more than a band with rifles is a smell in a clearing. Bayo's rule, correctly applied. It does not feel like a rule being correctly applied. ?][? if ch_res = "lev_hospital" : You carry out the instruments and the printing frame and leave a good deal of the ammunition in a cache you may or may not ever get back to. It is, militarily, the wrong choice, and everybody knows it and nobody argues, because a column that will burn its own hospital to carry bullets has already answered a question about itself that it would rather leave open. You march light and poor and you are still the thing that came up this mountain to do something. ?][? if ch_res = "lev_pueblo" : You do not burn it. You spend two days carrying it downhill — the maize, the tools, the medicines, the roofing sheets, the school benches, all of it into the villages — and you walk out of the camp with rifles and nothing else, and behind you eleven hamlets are quietly better off than they were on Monday. The soldiers arrive to a clearing containing ash and nothing worth photographing. In four valleys this becomes the story that gets told about the guerrilla: *when they had to leave, they gave everything away.* You have never been poorer and you have never been harder to dislodge. ?][? if ch_res = "tra_grande" : They walk in at dawn like men who have finally cornered something. Somebody picks up a pot. Somebody sits down on a bench in the school. And then the mountain comes apart under them, and it goes on coming apart for eleven minutes. It is the worst single morning the campaign in Guerrero has had and the corridos will still be arguing about the numbers in twenty years. The camp is gone by your own hand, which is the price of using your home as a weapon, and every person in this column would pay it again. ?][? if ch_res = "tra_ok" : You take them at the perimeter as the first section commits, which is smaller and surer than waiting, and it works cleanly: a bad ten minutes for them, no losses for you, and a withdrawal up the ridge in good order. The camp burns behind you either way. A modest, professional, entirely correct operation, and the only people disappointed are the ones who wanted the other thing. ?][? if ch_res = "tra_mal" : Somebody fires early — somebody always fires early, that is why patience is a statistic and not a virtue — and the trap half-springs into soldiers who go to ground much faster than expected. What follows is a firefight nobody planned, on ground you had already written off, and it costs four people to achieve less than walking away would have. The camp is gone. So are they. ?]

